From cb7b0b4baa8811ad3f8f9dc78bd9b71e25742a18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chriopter <82179548+chriopter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:39:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] ASoC: codecs: Add Everest ES7210 ADC driver

Add a driver for the Everest Semiconductor ES7210 4-channel audio ADC.
It supports the chip as clock consumer in the standard I2S, left
justified and DSP A/B formats, where ADC1/ADC2 are output on SDOUT1 and
ADC3/ADC4 on SDOUT2, with 16 to 32 bit samples and MCLK at a multiple of
256 fs.

The analog front end is powered up only while a capture stream runs.
The register sequences are taken from Everest's vendor driver and the
datasheet. Per-microphone PGA gain and digital volume are exposed as
controls.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig  |  14 ++
 sound/soc/codecs/Makefile |   2 +
 sound/soc/codecs/es7210.c | 495 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 511 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/codecs/es7210.c

